# AWS CI/CD Pipeline with Terraform, Jenkins, Docker, and GitHub

## Project Overview

This project demonstrates an end-to-end DevOps CI/CD pipeline built on AWS using Terraform, Jenkins, Docker, and GitHub.

The infrastructure is provisioned using Terraform, Jenkins is automatically installed on an EC2 instance, and application deployments are automated using Jenkins Pipelines and Docker.

---

## Architecture

Terraform
→ AWS VPC
→ Public Subnet
→ Internet Gateway
→ Route Table
→ Security Group
→ EC2 (Amazon Linux 2023)
→ Docker
→ Jenkins
→ GitHub Repository
→ Jenkinsfile
→ Docker Image Build
→ Container Deployment

---

## Technologies Used

* AWS EC2
* AWS VPC
* Terraform
* Jenkins
* Docker
* GitHub
* Linux (Amazon Linux 2023)
* Git
* Node.js

---

## Infrastructure Provisioned

Using Terraform, the following resources were created:

* VPC
* Public Subnet
* Internet Gateway
* Route Table
* Route Table Association
* Security Group
* EC2 Instance
* SSH Key Pair

---

## Jenkins Configuration

* Installed Jenkins using EC2 User Data
* Configured Java 21
* Installed Docker
* Added Jenkins user to Docker group
* Configured Jenkins Pipeline

---

## CI/CD Workflow

1. Developer pushes code to GitHub
2. Jenkins pulls source code
3. Jenkins reads Jenkinsfile
4. Docker image is built automatically
5. Existing container is removed
6. New container is deployed
7. Application becomes available on EC2

---

